IMPORT prelude

-- Disability Discrimination Act 1992 (Cth) -- the rules a person meets at work.
--
-- Based on content from the Federal Register of Legislation: "Disability Discrimination Act 1992", Compilation No. 40
-- (compilation date 1 July 2026, register id C2026C00276), Commonwealth of Australia, licensed under CC BY 4.0
-- (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Quotations are from the deposited plain-text conversion at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A04426.txt. Amendments commencing on or after 8 October 2026 are not in that text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Negatives follow the rulings of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05 (docs/ENCODING-GUIDE.md section 5): JUST FALSE where the
-- text itself says no; NOTHING where it does not answer, each tagged "NOTHING-kind" with the reason.

§ `Disability Discrimination Act 1992 -- work`

-- A MAYBE BOOLEAN conjunction. A no from the text in either part is a no; otherwise a part the text does not answer
-- leaves the whole unanswered.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`both` a b MEANS
    IF (a EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (b EQUALS JUST FALSE)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF (a EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (b EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 4 -- disability`

-- s 4(1) "disability, in relation to a person, means: (a) ... (g); and includes a disability that: (h) presently exists;
-- or (i) previously existed but no longer exists; or (j) may exist in the future (including because of a genetic
-- predisposition to that disability); or (k) is imputed to a person." Heads (h)-(k) widen when the condition counts,
-- never what kind of condition it is, so they are glossed in the question and not asked: a past, future, predisposed or
-- imputed condition of a kind in (a)-(g) is a disability. Behaviour that is a symptom of it is part of it.
DECLARE `Kind of condition` IS ONE OF
    `total or partial loss of bodily or mental functions`
    `total or partial loss of a part of the body`
    `organisms in the body causing disease or illness`
    `organisms in the body capable of causing disease or illness`
    `malfunction or malformation or disfigurement of a part of the body`
    `a disorder or malfunction that results in learning differently`
    `a disorder or illness or disease affecting thought processes or perception of reality or emotions or judgment or resulting in disturbed behaviour`
    `none of these`

-- A "means" definition: outside heads (a)-(g) the text says no.
GIVEN c IS A `Kind of condition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4 -- the condition is a disability` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `none of these` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 4 -- associate (with s 7)`

-- s 4(1) "associate, in relation to a person, includes: (a) a spouse of the person; and (b) another person who is living
-- with the person on a genuine domestic basis; and (c) a relative of the person; and (d) a carer of the person; and (e)
-- another person who is in a business, sporting or recreational relationship with the person." "relative ... means a
-- person who is related ... by blood, marriage, affinity or adoption." Head (d) runs one way: the person's own carer is
-- their associate; the person they care for is not named (finding 2).
DECLARE `Who the other person is to me` IS ONE OF
    `my spouse`
    `a person living with me on a genuine domestic basis`
    `my relative by blood or marriage or affinity or adoption`
    `my carer`
    `a person in a business or sporting or recreational relationship with me`
    `a person I care for who is not my relative`
    `someone else`

GIVEN w IS A `Who the other person is to me`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4 -- the person is my associate` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    -- NOTHING-kind: the list "includes" and is not closed; the person I care for is not named in it.
    WHEN `a person I care for who is not my relative` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind: the list "includes" and is not closed.
    WHEN `someone else` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 9 -- carer, assistant, assistance animal, disability aid (with s 8)`

DECLARE `What assists me` IS ONE OF
    `a carer`
    `an assistant`
    `an interpreter`
    `a reader`
    `another kind of helper`
    `an animal`
    `equipment`

DECLARE `Section 9 facts` HAS
    `what it is`                      IS A `What assists me`
    `helps because of the disability` IS A BOOLEAN
    `animal accredited under State or Territory law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `animal accredited by a prescribed organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `animal trained to alleviate the disability`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `animal trained for public hygiene and behaviour` IS A BOOLEAN
    `equipment used by me`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `equipment alleviates the disability` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 9(1) "a carer or assistant ... is one of the following who provides assistance or services to the person because of
-- the disability: (a) a carer; (b) an assistant; (c) an interpreter; (d) a reader." A closed list ("is one of").
-- s 9(2) "an assistance animal is a dog or other animal: (a) accredited under a law of a State or Territory ...; or (b)
-- accredited by an animal training organisation prescribed by the regulations ...; or (c) trained: (i) to assist a person
-- with a disability to alleviate the effect of the disability; and (ii) to meet standards of hygiene and behaviour that
-- are appropriate for an animal in a public place." The prescribed organisations are in regulations not deposited, so
-- (b) is asked as a fact.
-- s 9(3) "a disability aid ... is equipment (including a palliative or therapeutic device) that: (a) is used by the
-- person; and (b) provides assistance to alleviate the effect of the disability."
-- s 9(4): the person "has" one if accompanied by it now, before, in future, or imputed; glossed in the question.
GIVEN f IS A `Section 9 facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9 -- the Act counts what assists me` f MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `what it is`
    WHEN `another kind of helper` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an animal` THEN
        JUST (    f's `animal accredited under State or Territory law`
              OR f's `animal accredited by a prescribed organisation`
              OR (f's `animal trained to alleviate the disability` AND f's `animal trained for public hygiene and behaviour`))
    WHEN `equipment` THEN
        JUST (f's `equipment used by me` AND f's `equipment alleviates the disability`)
    OTHERWISE JUST (f's `helps because of the disability`)

§§ `ss 7, 8 -- whose disability, or what, the treatment was about`

DECLARE `The ground` IS ONE OF
    `my own disability`
    `my carer or assistant or assistance animal or disability aid`
    `the disability of an associate of mine`

-- s 7(1) "This Act applies in relation to a person who has an associate with a disability in the same way as it applies
-- in relation to a person with the disability." s 8(1) "This Act applies in relation to having a carer, assistant,
-- assistance animal or disability aid in the same way as it applies in relation to having a disability."
-- The condition c is the disability of whoever has it: mine, or my associate's.
GIVEN g IS A `The ground`, c IS A `Kind of condition`, w IS A `Who the other person is to me`, f IS A `Section 9 facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 4, 7, 8, 9 -- the ground is one the Act covers` g c w f MEANS
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `my own disability` THEN `s 4 -- the condition is a disability` c
    WHEN `my carer or assistant or assistance animal or disability aid` THEN
        `both` (`s 4 -- the condition is a disability` c) (`s 9 -- the Act counts what assists me` f)
    WHEN `the disability of an associate of mine` THEN
        `both` (`s 4 -- the person is my associate` w) (`s 4 -- the condition is a disability` c)

§§ `ss 5, 6, 10, 11 -- what discrimination is`

-- Each fact is a judgment for the tribunal or court, asked as an input and never decided here.
DECLARE `Discrimination facts` HAS
    `less favourable treatment`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `disability one of the reasons`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `adjustments not made`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `hardship of adjusting shown`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `not adjusting led to worse treatment`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `requirement imposed`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `cannot comply because of the disability` IS A BOOLEAN
    `could comply only with adjustments`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `disadvantages persons with the disability` IS A BOOLEAN
    `requirement shown reasonable`          IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 5(1): "because of the disability, the discriminator treats, or proposes to treat, the aggrieved person less
-- favourably than the discriminator would treat a person without the disability in circumstances that are not materially
-- different." s 5(3): needing adjustments does not make the circumstances materially different. s 10: the disability
-- need only be one of two or more reasons, "whether or not it is the dominant or a substantial reason".
GIVEN f IS A `Discrimination facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(1) -- less favourable treatment because of the disability` f IF
        f's `less favourable treatment`
    AND f's `disability one of the reasons`

-- s 5(2): "(a) the discriminator does not make, or proposes not to make, reasonable adjustments for the person; and (b)
-- the failure ... has, or would have, the effect that the aggrieved person is, because of the disability, treated less
-- favourably". s 4(1): "an adjustment ... is a reasonable adjustment unless making the adjustment would impose an
-- unjustifiable hardship on the person"; s 11(2): the burden of proving the hardship lies on the person claiming it.
GIVEN f IS A `Discrimination facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(2) -- failure to make reasonable adjustments` f IF
        f's `adjustments not made`
    AND (NOT f's `hardship of adjusting shown`)
    AND f's `not adjusting led to worse treatment`

-- s 6(1): a requirement or condition the person, because of the disability, does not or cannot comply with, which has or
-- is likely to have the effect of disadvantaging persons with the disability. s 6(3), (4): not if the requirement is
-- reasonable in the circumstances, the burden of proving that lying on the person who imposes it.
GIVEN f IS A `Discrimination facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 6(1) -- a requirement I cannot comply with` f IF
        f's `requirement imposed`
    AND f's `cannot comply because of the disability`
    AND f's `disadvantages persons with the disability`
    AND (NOT f's `requirement shown reasonable`)

-- s 6(2): the person "would comply, or would be able to comply, with the requirement or condition only if the
-- discriminator made reasonable adjustments for the person, but the discriminator does not do so", and the failure has or
-- is likely to have the effect of disadvantaging persons with the disability; s 6(3), (4) as above.
GIVEN f IS A `Discrimination facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 6(2) -- a requirement I could meet only with reasonable adjustments` f IF
        f's `requirement imposed`
    AND f's `could comply only with adjustments`
    AND f's `adjustments not made`
    AND (NOT f's `hardship of adjusting shown`)
    AND f's `disadvantages persons with the disability`
    AND (NOT f's `requirement shown reasonable`)

-- s 4(1) "discriminate has the meaning given by sections 5 and 6": a closed definition, so outside its four limbs the
-- text says no.
GIVEN f IS A `Discrimination facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 5, 6 -- they discriminated` f IF
       `s 5(1) -- less favourable treatment because of the disability` f
    OR `s 5(2) -- failure to make reasonable adjustments` f
    OR `s 6(1) -- a requirement I cannot comply with` f
    OR `s 6(2) -- a requirement I could meet only with reasonable adjustments` f

§§ `Part 2 Division 1 -- discrimination in work (ss 15-21)`

DECLARE `My position at work` IS ONE OF
    `seeking employment`
    `an employee`
    `seeking to be engaged as a commission agent`
    `a commission agent`
    `a contract worker`
    `seeking to become a partner`
    `a partner`
    `seeking or holding an authorisation or qualification for my profession or trade or occupation`
    `applying to join a registered organisation`
    `a member of a registered organisation`
    `a person using an employment agency`

DECLARE `What was done` IS ONE OF
    `the arrangements made for deciding who is offered the work`
    `deciding who is offered the work`
    `the terms or conditions on which the work or position is offered`
    `the terms or conditions of my work or position`
    `deciding who is offered promotion or transfer`
    `denying or limiting my access to promotion or transfer or training or other benefits`
    `dismissing me or ending my engagement or position or membership`
    `subjecting me to any other detriment`
    `refusing or failing to grant or renew or extend or accept`
    `the manner in which a service is provided to me`

-- Each of ss 15-21 lists the acts it makes unlawful. A pairing of position and act that no paragraph lists is outside
-- the prohibition's own wording: NOTHING-kind (scope limit), so every OTHERWISE NOTHING below carries that tag.

-- s 15(1) (a) arrangements, (b) determining who should be offered employment, (c) terms on which offered.
GIVEN a IS A `What was done`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 15(1) -- the paragraph` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `the arrangements made for deciding who is offered the work` THEN JUST "s 15(1)(a)"
    WHEN `deciding who is offered the work` THEN JUST "s 15(1)(b)"
    WHEN `the terms or conditions on which the work or position is offered` THEN JUST "s 15(1)(c)"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 15(2) (a) terms or conditions of employment, (b) denying or limiting access to promotion, transfer, training or other
-- benefits, (c) dismissing, (d) any other detriment. s 16(2) is the same for a commission agent ("terminating the
-- engagement").
GIVEN `the section` IS A STRING, a IS A `What was done`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`ss 15(2), 16(2) -- the paragraph` `the section` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `the terms or conditions of my work or position` THEN JUST (CONCAT `the section`, "(a)")
    WHEN `deciding who is offered promotion or transfer` THEN JUST (CONCAT `the section`, "(b)")
    WHEN `denying or limiting my access to promotion or transfer or training or other benefits` THEN JUST (CONCAT `the section`, "(b)")
    WHEN `dismissing me or ending my engagement or position or membership` THEN JUST (CONCAT `the section`, "(c)")
    WHEN `subjecting me to any other detriment` THEN JUST (CONCAT `the section`, "(d)")
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 16(1) (a) arrangements, (b) determining who should be engaged, (c) terms on which engaged.
GIVEN a IS A `What was done`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 16(1) -- the paragraph` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `the arrangements made for deciding who is offered the work` THEN JUST "s 16(1)(a)"
    WHEN `deciding who is offered the work` THEN JUST "s 16(1)(b)"
    WHEN `the terms or conditions on which the work or position is offered` THEN JUST "s 16(1)(c)"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 17 (a) terms on which the principal allows the contract worker to work, (b) not allowing the contract worker to work
-- or continue to work, (c) denying or limiting access to any benefit associated with the work, (d) any other detriment.
-- Not being allowed to start work is read as (b) (fork F3).
GIVEN a IS A `What was done`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 17 -- the paragraph` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `the terms or conditions of my work or position` THEN JUST "s 17(a)"
    WHEN `deciding who is offered the work` THEN JUST "s 17(b)"
    WHEN `dismissing me or ending my engagement or position or membership` THEN JUST "s 17(b)"
    WHEN `deciding who is offered promotion or transfer` THEN JUST "s 17(c)"
    WHEN `denying or limiting my access to promotion or transfer or training or other benefits` THEN JUST "s 17(c)"
    WHEN `subjecting me to any other detriment` THEN JUST "s 17(d)"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 18(1) "3 or more persons who are proposing to form themselves into a partnership", s 18(2) "a partnership consisting
-- of 3 or more partners": (a) determining who should be invited to become a partner, (b) terms of the invitation.
-- s 18(3) (a) denying or limiting access to a benefit of being a partner, (b) expelling, (c) any other detriment.
-- Fewer than 3: outside the section's own scope, NOTHING-kind (scope limit, ruling of 2026-11-05 (c)).
GIVEN `the partner` IS A BOOLEAN, n IS A NUMBER, a IS A `What was done`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 18 -- the paragraph` `the partner` n a MEANS
    IF n LESS THAN 3
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the partner`
         THEN CONSIDER a
              WHEN `denying or limiting my access to promotion or transfer or training or other benefits` THEN JUST "s 18(3)(a)"
              WHEN `dismissing me or ending my engagement or position or membership` THEN JUST "s 18(3)(b)"
              WHEN `subjecting me to any other detriment` THEN JUST "s 18(3)(c)"
              OTHERWISE NOTHING
         ELSE CONSIDER a
              WHEN `deciding who is offered the work` THEN JUST "s 18(1)(a) or (2)(a)"
              WHEN `the terms or conditions on which the work or position is offered` THEN JUST "s 18(1)(b) or (2)(b)"
              OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 19 (a) refusing or failing to confer, renew or extend the authorisation or qualification, (b) the terms on which it
-- is conferred, renewed or extended, (c) revoking or withdrawing it or varying the terms on which it is held.
GIVEN a IS A `What was done`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 19 -- the paragraph` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `refusing or failing to grant or renew or extend or accept` THEN JUST "s 19(a)"
    WHEN `the terms or conditions on which the work or position is offered` THEN JUST "s 19(b)"
    WHEN `the terms or conditions of my work or position` THEN JUST "s 19(c)"
    WHEN `dismissing me or ending my engagement or position or membership` THEN JUST "s 19(c)"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 20(1) (a) refusing or failing to accept the application for membership, (b) the terms of admission.
-- s 20(2) (a) denying or limiting access to a benefit, (b) depriving of membership or varying its terms, (c) any other
-- detriment.
GIVEN `a member` IS A BOOLEAN, a IS A `What was done`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 20 -- the paragraph` `a member` a MEANS
    IF `a member`
    THEN CONSIDER a
         WHEN `denying or limiting my access to promotion or transfer or training or other benefits` THEN JUST "s 20(2)(a)"
         WHEN `dismissing me or ending my engagement or position or membership` THEN JUST "s 20(2)(b)"
         WHEN `the terms or conditions of my work or position` THEN JUST "s 20(2)(b)"
         WHEN `subjecting me to any other detriment` THEN JUST "s 20(2)(c)"
         OTHERWISE NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER a
         WHEN `refusing or failing to grant or renew or extend or accept` THEN JUST "s 20(1)(a)"
         WHEN `the terms or conditions on which the work or position is offered` THEN JUST "s 20(1)(b)"
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 21(1) (a) refusing to provide any of its services, (b) the terms on which it offers them, (c) the manner in which it
-- provides them.
GIVEN a IS A `What was done`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 21 -- the paragraph` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `refusing or failing to grant or renew or extend or accept` THEN JUST "s 21(1)(a)"
    WHEN `the terms or conditions on which the work or position is offered` THEN JUST "s 21(1)(b)"
    WHEN `the manner in which a service is provided to me` THEN JUST "s 21(1)(c)"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The paragraph of ss 15-21 that lists what was done, for my position; n is the number of partners (or persons proposing
-- to form the partnership), read only for s 18.
GIVEN p IS A `My position at work`, a IS A `What was done`, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`ss 15-21 -- the paragraph that covers what was done` p a n MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `seeking employment` THEN `s 15(1) -- the paragraph` a
    WHEN `an employee` THEN `ss 15(2), 16(2) -- the paragraph` "s 15(2)" a
    WHEN `seeking to be engaged as a commission agent` THEN `s 16(1) -- the paragraph` a
    WHEN `a commission agent` THEN `ss 15(2), 16(2) -- the paragraph` "s 16(2)" a
    WHEN `a contract worker` THEN `s 17 -- the paragraph` a
    WHEN `seeking to become a partner` THEN `s 18 -- the paragraph` FALSE n a
    WHEN `a partner` THEN `s 18 -- the paragraph` TRUE n a
    WHEN `seeking or holding an authorisation or qualification for my profession or trade or occupation` THEN `s 19 -- the paragraph` a
    WHEN `applying to join a registered organisation` THEN `s 20 -- the paragraph` FALSE a
    WHEN `a member of a registered organisation` THEN `s 20 -- the paragraph` TRUE a
    WHEN `a person using an employment agency` THEN `s 21 -- the paragraph` a

GIVEN p IS A `My position at work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20 -- my position is with a registered organisation` p IF
       p EQUALS `applying to join a registered organisation`
    OR p EQUALS `a member of a registered organisation`

§§ `s 12 -- how far the Act reaches`

DECLARE `Reach facts` HAS
    `done in a Territory`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `Commonwealth employment`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `qualification under a Commonwealth law`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `done by the Commonwealth using its powers`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a treaty head accepted`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `done by a foreign or trading or financial corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the business of banking or insurance`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `in interstate or overseas trade or commerce` IS A BOOLEAN
    `involving matters outside Australia`         IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 12(1): "limited application provisions means the provisions of Divisions 1, 2, 2A and 3 of Part 2 other than
-- sections 20, 29 and 30." s 12(4): they "have effect as provided in subsection (3) ... and the following provisions of
-- this section and not otherwise" -- a closed list, so outside every head the text says no.
-- (3) acts done within a Territory ("Territory ... does not include the Australian Capital Territory and the Northern
-- Territory", s 4(1)); (5) ss 15, 16 and 17 for Commonwealth employees and persons seeking to become one; (6) s 19 for an
-- authority exercising a power under a Commonwealth law; (7) acts by the Commonwealth, a Territory Administration or a
-- Commonwealth or Territory statutory body in the exercise of a Commonwealth or Territory power; (8) to the extent the
-- provisions give effect to the ILO Convention 111, the ICCPR, the Disabilities Convention or the ICESCR, or relate to
-- matters external to Australia or of international concern -- a constitutional judgment, asked conditionally; (9), (10)
-- foreign, trading or financial corporations and their officers and employees in the course of their duties; (11)
-- banking and insurance other than State banking or insurance within one State; (12) overseas and interstate trade or
-- commerce; (13), (14) matters arising outside Australia.
-- `in Division 3` is TRUE for harassment (s 35), where heads (5) and (6) do not apply.
GIVEN p IS A `My position at work`, `in Division 3` IS A BOOLEAN, r IS A `Reach facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 12 -- the Act reaches what was done` p `in Division 3` r IF
       ((NOT `in Division 3`) AND `s 20 -- my position is with a registered organisation` p)
    OR r's `done in a Territory`
    OR ((NOT `in Division 3`) AND r's `Commonwealth employment` AND `s 12(5) -- a section 15, 16 or 17 position` p)
    OR ((NOT `in Division 3`) AND r's `qualification under a Commonwealth law` AND (p EQUALS `seeking or holding an authorisation or qualification for my profession or trade or occupation`))
    OR r's `done by the Commonwealth using its powers`
    OR r's `a treaty head accepted`
    OR r's `done by a foreign or trading or financial corporation`
    OR r's `in the business of banking or insurance`
    OR r's `in interstate or overseas trade or commerce`
    OR r's `involving matters outside Australia`
    WHERE
        GIVEN q IS A `My position at work`
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        DECIDE `s 12(5) -- a section 15, 16 or 17 position` q IF
               q EQUALS `seeking employment`
            OR q EQUALS `an employee`
            OR q EQUALS `seeking to be engaged as a commission agent`
            OR q EQUALS `a commission agent`
            OR q EQUALS `a contract worker`

§§ `ss 15(3), 21A, 21B -- the exceptions in Division 1`

-- s 15(3): "Neither paragraph (1)(a) nor (b) renders it unlawful ... in connection with employment to perform domestic
-- duties on the premises on which the first-mentioned person resides." A flat negative.
GIVEN p IS A `My position at work`, a IS A `What was done`, `domestic duties at their home` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 15(3) -- domestic duties in the employer's home` p a `domestic duties at their home` IF
        p EQUALS `seeking employment`
    AND `domestic duties at their home`
    AND (   a EQUALS `the arrangements made for deciding who is offered the work`
         OR a EQUALS `deciding who is offered the work`)

-- s 21A(4): "This section does not apply in relation to: (a) discrimination referred to in paragraph 15(2)(b) or (d),
-- 16(2)(b) or (d), 17(c) or (d) or 18(3)(c), other than discrimination in determining who should be offered promotion or
-- transfer; or (b) discrimination referred to in section 20".
GIVEN p IS A `My position at work`, a IS A `What was done`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21A(4) -- the inherent requirements exception does not apply` p a IF
       `s 20 -- my position is with a registered organisation` p
    OR (    (p EQUALS `an employee` OR p EQUALS `a commission agent` OR p EQUALS `a contract worker`)
        AND (   a EQUALS `denying or limiting my access to promotion or transfer or training or other benefits`
             OR a EQUALS `subjecting me to any other detriment`))
    OR (p EQUALS `a partner` AND a EQUALS `subjecting me to any other detriment`)

-- s 21A(1): not unlawful if "(a) the discrimination relates to particular work (including promotion or transfer to
-- particular work); and (b) because of the disability, the aggrieved person would be unable to carry out the inherent
-- requirements of the particular work, even if the relevant employer, principal or partnership made reasonable
-- adjustments". (b) is a judgment taking in the s 21A(2) factors (training, qualifications, experience, past performance),
-- asked as an input.
GIVEN p IS A `My position at work`, a IS A `What was done`,
      `relates to particular work` IS A BOOLEAN, `unable to carry out the inherent requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21A -- the inherent requirements exception applies` p a `relates to particular work` `unable to carry out the inherent requirements` IF
        `relates to particular work`
    AND `unable to carry out the inherent requirements`
    AND (NOT `s 21A(4) -- the inherent requirements exception does not apply` p a)

-- s 21B: not unlawful "if avoiding the discrimination would impose an unjustifiable hardship on the discriminator"; s 11:
-- all relevant circumstances, the burden on the person claiming it (s 11(2)). Asked as an input.

§§ `Part 2 Division 5 -- exemptions that reach work`

DECLARE `Exemption facts` HAS
    `special measure`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `discrimination not necessary for the measure` IS A BOOLEAN
    `about rates of salary or wages`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `about insurance or superannuation`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `based on reasonable actuarial or statistical data` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable given the data and other factors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `no data available or obtainable`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable given other factors`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `complying with a court order`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `complying with capacity-based wage provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `complying with a prescribed law`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disability is an infectious disease` IS A BOOLEAN
    `necessary to protect public health`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `Migration Act permits or requires it`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `Defence Force combat or peacekeeping position` IS A BOOLEAN
    `selection for a peacekeeping force`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `animal suspected of infectious disease`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `necessary to protect health of people or animals` IS A BOOLEAN
    `animal evidence asked for and not produced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acting under a Commission exemption`     IS A BOOLEAN

-- The first exemption that applies, in the order of Division 5, or "none". Each is a flat negative ("This Part does not
-- render it unlawful ..."). s 49 (charities' governing rules), s 51 (pensions under listed Acts) and s 54A(2), (5), (7)
-- are out of scope (NOTES.md).
GIVEN e IS A `Exemption facts`, g IS A `The ground`, f IS A `Section 9 facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`Division 5 -- the exemption that applies` e g f MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- s 45(1), (2): an act reasonably intended to ensure equal opportunities or to meet special needs, but not
        -- discrimination not necessary for the measure, and not rates of salary or wages.
        IF      e's `special measure`
            AND (NOT e's `discrimination not necessary for the measure`)
            AND (NOT e's `about rates of salary or wages`)
        THEN "s 45 (special measures)"
        -- s 46(1), (2): refusing to offer, or the terms of, an annuity, life or other insurance policy, or membership of
        -- a superannuation or provident fund or scheme, (f) based on actuarial or statistical data reasonable to rely on
        -- and reasonable having regard to it and other factors, or (g) where no such data is available or reasonably
        -- obtainable, reasonable having regard to other factors.
        IF      e's `about insurance or superannuation`
            AND (   (e's `based on reasonable actuarial or statistical data` AND e's `reasonable given the data and other factors`)
                 OR (e's `no data available or obtainable` AND e's `reasonable given other factors`))
        THEN "s 46 (superannuation and insurance)"
        -- s 47(1)(b) a court order; (1)(c), (d) an industrial instrument or minimum-wage order with specific provisions for
        -- capacity-based wages of persons who would otherwise be eligible for the disability support pension; (2) a
        -- prescribed law (regulations not deposited: asked).
        IF e's `complying with a court order` OR e's `complying with capacity-based wage provisions` OR e's `complying with a prescribed law`
        THEN "s 47 (acts done under statutory authority)"
        -- s 48: the disability is an infectious disease and the discrimination is reasonably necessary to protect public
        -- health. s 8(3): s 48 does not apply to the carer, assistant, animal or aid ground.
        IF      e's `the disability is an infectious disease`
            AND e's `necessary to protect public health`
            AND (NOT (g EQUALS `my carer or assistant or assistance animal or disability aid`))
        THEN "s 48 (infectious diseases)"
        -- s 52: Divisions 1, 2 and 2A do not render unlawful anything permitted or required by the Migration Act 1958 or
        -- an instrument under it.
        IF e's `Migration Act permits or requires it`
        THEN "s 52 (migration)"
        -- s 53: Defence Force positions involving combat, combat-related duties or peacekeeping service, prescribed
        -- circumstances, chaplains and medical support persons. s 7(3): not for associates.
        IF e's `Defence Force combat or peacekeeping position` AND (NOT (g EQUALS `the disability of an associate of mine`))
        THEN "s 53 (combat duties and peacekeeping services)"
        -- s 54: selection for peacekeeping duties as part of a Peacekeeping Force. s 7(3): not for associates.
        IF e's `selection for a peacekeeping force` AND (NOT (g EQUALS `the disability of an associate of mine`))
        THEN "s 54 (peacekeeping services by the AFP)"
        -- s 54A(4): the person has an assistance animal, the discriminator reasonably suspects it has an infectious disease
        -- and the discrimination is reasonably necessary to protect public health or the health of other animals.
        IF      `I have an assistance animal`
            AND e's `animal suspected of infectious disease`
            AND e's `necessary to protect health of people or animals`
        THEN "s 54A(4) (assistance animal with an infectious disease)"
        -- s 54A(6): discrimination on the ground that the person has the assistance animal, where evidence that it is an
        -- assistance animal or is trained for a public place was asked for and neither was produced.
        IF      `I have an assistance animal`
            AND (g EQUALS `my carer or assistant or assistance animal or disability aid`)
            AND e's `animal evidence asked for and not produced`
        THEN "s 54A(6) (no evidence about the assistance animal)"
        -- s 58: an act in accordance with an exemption granted by the Commission under s 55 (at most 5 years, s 55(3)(c)).
        IF e's `acting under a Commission exemption`
        THEN "s 58 (an exemption granted by the Commission)"
        OTHERWISE "none"
    WHERE
        `I have an assistance animal` MEANS
                (f's `what it is` EQUALS `an animal`)
            AND (`s 9 -- the Act counts what assists me` f EQUALS JUST TRUE)

§§ `Division 1 -- the whole question`

DECLARE `What the Act says about what was done to me at work` IS ONE OF
    `unlawful discrimination under` HAS `the provision` IS A STRING
    `not unlawful: outside the reach of the Act (s 12)`
    `not unlawful: an exception or exemption applies` HAS `the exception` IS A STRING
    `not discrimination as sections 5 and 6 define it`
    `not on a ground the Act covers`
    `not shown to be on a ground the Act covers`
    `not an act that sections 15 to 21 list for my position`

-- The questions in the order a tribunal would meet them: which paragraph lists the act; the ground; whether it is
-- discrimination; the reach; then the exceptions (ss 15(3), 21A, 21B) and the exemptions of Division 5.
GIVEN p IS A `My position at work`, a IS A `What was done`, n IS A NUMBER, `domestic` IS A BOOLEAN,
      g IS A `The ground`, c IS A `Kind of condition`, w IS A `Who the other person is to me`, f9 IS A `Section 9 facts`,
      d IS A `Discrimination facts`, r IS A `Reach facts`,
      `particular work` IS A BOOLEAN, `unable` IS A BOOLEAN, `hardship to avoid shown` IS A BOOLEAN,
      e IS A `Exemption facts`
GIVETH A `What the Act says about what was done to me at work`
`Division 1 -- what the Act says` p a n `domestic` g c w f9 d r `particular work` `unable` `hardship to avoid shown` e MEANS
    CONSIDER `ss 15-21 -- the paragraph that covers what was done` p a n
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `not an act that sections 15 to 21 list for my position`
    WHEN JUST `the paragraph` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `the ground` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN `not on a ground the Act covers`
            IF `the ground` EQUALS NOTHING THEN `not shown to be on a ground the Act covers`
            IF NOT (`ss 5, 6 -- they discriminated` d) THEN `not discrimination as sections 5 and 6 define it`
            IF NOT (`s 12 -- the Act reaches what was done` p FALSE r) THEN `not unlawful: outside the reach of the Act (s 12)`
            IF `s 15(3) -- domestic duties in the employer's home` p a `domestic` THEN `not unlawful: an exception or exemption applies` "s 15(3) (domestic duties in the employer's home)"
            IF `s 21A -- the inherent requirements exception applies` p a `particular work` `unable` THEN `not unlawful: an exception or exemption applies` "s 21A (inherent requirements)"
            IF `hardship to avoid shown` THEN `not unlawful: an exception or exemption applies` "s 21B (unjustifiable hardship)"
            IF NOT (`the exemption` EQUALS "none") THEN `not unlawful: an exception or exemption applies` `the exemption`
            OTHERWISE `unlawful discrimination under` `the paragraph`
    WHERE
        `the ground` MEANS `ss 4, 7, 8, 9 -- the ground is one the Act covers` g c w f9
        `the exemption` MEANS `Division 5 -- the exemption that applies` e g f9

-- The same, as yes, no or not answered. Yes: unlawful. No (the text's own no): outside the reach (s 12(4) "and not
-- otherwise"), or an exception or exemption ("does not render it unlawful"). Not answered (NOTHING-kind: the prohibition
-- is limited in its own wording and the case falls outside it): not discrimination, not on a covered ground, or an act
-- not listed for the position.
GIVEN o IS A `What the Act says about what was done to me at work`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Division 1 -- unlawful` o MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `unlawful discrimination under` x THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `not unlawful: outside the reach of the Act (s 12)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `not unlawful: an exception or exemption applies` x THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 35 -- harassment in employment`

DECLARE `Who harassed me` IS ONE OF
    `my employer`
    `a person employed by my employer`
    `a person I was seeking employment with or a person employed by that employer`
    `the person I work for as a commission agent or contract worker`
    `a fellow commission agent or contract worker of the same principal`
    `a person I was seeking to work for as a commission agent or contract worker or their agent or contract worker`
    `someone else`

-- s 35(1)-(6): "It is unlawful for a person to harass another person who: (a) [stands in one of six relations to the
-- harasser]; and (b) has a disability; in relation to the disability." "harass" is not defined: asked. Division 1's
-- exceptions (ss 21A, 21B) say "This Division" and do not reach s 35 (finding 4). s 7 carries the associate's disability
-- across ("in the same way").
GIVEN h IS A `Who harassed me`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 35 -- the subsection` h MEANS
    CONSIDER h
    WHEN `my employer` THEN JUST "s 35(1)"
    WHEN `a person employed by my employer` THEN JUST "s 35(2)"
    WHEN `a person I was seeking employment with or a person employed by that employer` THEN JUST "s 35(3)"
    WHEN `the person I work for as a commission agent or contract worker` THEN JUST "s 35(4)"
    WHEN `a fellow commission agent or contract worker of the same principal` THEN JUST "s 35(5)"
    WHEN `a person I was seeking to work for as a commission agent or contract worker or their agent or contract worker` THEN JUST "s 35(6)"
    -- NOTHING-kind: the six relations limit the prohibition in its own wording (a customer, a client, a stranger).
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN h IS A `Who harassed me`, `harassed in relation to the disability` IS A BOOLEAN,
      g IS A `The ground`, c IS A `Kind of condition`, w IS A `Who the other person is to me`, f9 IS A `Section 9 facts`,
      r IS A `Reach facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35 -- the harassment is unlawful` h `harassed in relation to the disability` g c w f9 r MEANS
    IF `s 35 -- the subsection` h EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind: no covered ground, or no harassment in relation to it -- outside the prohibition's own wording.
    ELSE IF NOT (`ss 4, 7, 8, 9 -- the ground is one the Act covers` g c w f9 EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF NOT `harassed in relation to the disability`
              THEN NOTHING
              ELSE JUST (`s 12 -- the Act reaches what was done` `seeking employment` TRUE r)

§§ `ss 42, 58A -- victimisation`

DECLARE `What I did` IS ONE OF
    `made or proposed to make a complaint under this Act or the Australian Human Rights Commission Act`
    `brought or proposed to bring proceedings under either Act`
    `gave or proposed to give information or documents to a person exercising powers under either Act`
    `attended or proposed to attend a conference held under either Act`
    `appeared or proposed to appear as a witness in a proceeding under either Act`
    `reasonably asserted rights under either Act`
    `proposed to assert rights under either Act`
    `alleged that someone did an act unlawful under Part 2`
    `none of these`

-- s 58A(2) and s 42(2): an act of victimisation is subjecting, or threatening to subject, the other person to any
-- detriment "on the ground that the other person" did or proposes to do one of (a)-(g), "or on the ground that the first
-- person believes that the other person has done, or proposes to do," one of them. (f) reads "has reasonably asserted, or
-- proposes to assert": "reasonably" qualifies only the past assertion (finding 5).
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `What I did`, `they believed I did one` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `detriment or threat` IS A BOOLEAN, `on that ground` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 58A(2) -- an act of victimisation` `what I did` `they believed I did one` `detriment or threat` `on that ground` IF
        `detriment or threat`
    AND `on that ground`
    AND (    (NOT (`what I did` EQUALS `none of these`))
         OR `they believed I did one`)

DECLARE `Victimisation party` IS ONE OF `the other person`
DECLARE `Victimisation act` IS ONE OF `subject me or threaten me with a detriment for a protected act`

-- s 58A(1) "It is unlawful for a person to commit an act of victimisation against another person." A prohibition with no
-- period of its own: the WITHIN is the one period the question asks about (one unit), so that a trace with no act ends
-- FULFILLED and one with the act ends in BREACH.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Victimisation party` `Victimisation act`
`s 58A(1) -- the other person must not victimise me` MEANS
    PARTY `the other person`
    SHANT `subject me or threaten me with a detriment for a protected act`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST BREACH BY `the other person` BECAUSE "victimisation: unlawful under s 58A and an offence under s 42 punishable by imprisonment for 6 months"

-- Runs the prohibition over what happened. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE matches FULFILLED but not BREACH,
-- so anything other than FULFILLED is the breach. It takes no DEONTIC input and is not exported.
GIVEN `it happened` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 58A(1) -- the prohibition was kept` `it happened` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 58A(1) -- the other person must not victimise me` 0 `the events`
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        `the events` MEANS
            IF `it happened`
            THEN LIST (EVENT `the other person` `subject me or threaten me with a detriment for a protected act` 0), (WAITUNTIL 2)
            ELSE LIST (WAITUNTIL 2)

-- s 42(1): "It is an offence for a person to commit an act of victimisation against another person. Penalty:
-- Imprisonment for 6 months." s 123(5): a person other than a body corporate convicted only because of s 123(3) and (4)
-- (conduct of their employee or agent) "is not liable to be punished by imprisonment".
GIVEN `victimised` IS A BOOLEAN, `liable only through an employee or agent and not a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 42 -- the most months of imprisonment` `victimised` `liable only through an employee or agent and not a company` MEANS
    IF NOT `victimised`
    THEN JUST 0
    ELSE IF `liable only through an employee or agent and not a company`
         THEN JUST 0
         ELSE JUST 6

§§ `s 44 -- advertisements`

-- s 44(1): an offence to publish or display, or cause or permit to be published or displayed, an advertisement or notice
-- that indicates, or could reasonably be understood as indicating, an intention to do an act unlawful under Division 1,
-- 2, 2A or 3. "Penalty: 10 penalty units." The value of a penalty unit is set by the Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA, not deposited.
GIVEN `published by them or with their permission` IS A BOOLEAN, `indicates an intention to discriminate unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 44 -- the most penalty units for the advertisement` `published by them or with their permission` `indicates an intention to discriminate unlawfully` MEANS
    IF `published by them or with their permission` AND `indicates an intention to discriminate unlawfully`
    THEN JUST 10
    -- NOTHING-kind: s 44 limits the offence in its own wording; it does not say other advertisements are lawful.
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ss 122, 123 -- who else is answerable`

-- s 122: "A person who causes, instructs, induces, aids or permits another person to do an act that is unlawful under
-- Division 1, 2, 2A, 3 or 6 of Part 2 is, for the purposes of this Act, taken also to have done the act."
GIVEN `they caused instructed induced aided or permitted it` IS A BOOLEAN, `the act is unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 122 -- they are taken to have done the act` `they caused instructed induced aided or permitted it` `the act is unlawful` MEANS
    IF `they caused instructed induced aided or permitted it` AND `the act is unlawful`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind: s 122 is a deeming rule; it is silent on anyone outside it.
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 123(2), (4): conduct "engaged in on behalf of" a body corporate or other person "by a director, employee or agent ...
-- within the scope of his or her actual or apparent authority is taken ... to have been engaged in also by" them "unless"
-- they establish "that [they] took reasonable precautions and exercised due diligence to avoid the conduct".
-- Fork F6: once the "unless" is met, the answer taken is JUST FALSE (the deeming is displaced in the text's own words).
GIVEN `within actual or apparent authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonable precautions and due diligence established` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 123 -- the employer is taken to have done it` `within actual or apparent authority` `reasonable precautions and due diligence established` MEANS
    IF NOT `within actual or apparent authority`
    -- NOTHING-kind: outside the scope of authority s 123 does not deem; s 122 may still apply.
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (NOT `reasonable precautions and due diligence established`)

§§ `s 13(4) -- a complaint already made under a State or Territory law`

-- s 13(4): if a State or Territory discrimination law deals with the matter and the person "has made a complaint or
-- initiated a proceeding under that law" about the act, "the person is not entitled to make a complaint or institute a
-- proceeding under the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986 alleging that the act or omission is unlawful under a
-- provision of Part 2 of this Act."
GIVEN `the State law deals with the matter` IS A BOOLEAN, `I complained or sued under it about the same act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 13(4) -- I am barred from a complaint under this Act` `the State law deals with the matter` `I complained or sued under it about the same act` IF
        `the State law deals with the matter`
    AND `I complained or sued under it about the same act`
